{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And He formed.</b> Two formations — a formation for this world and a formation for the resurrection of the dead. But for the beast, which does not stand for judgment, two yods were not written in its formation." "<b>Dust from the earth.</b> He gathered his dust from all the earth, from the four winds, so that wherever he dies, there [the earth] receives him for burial. Another interpretation: He took his dust from the place of which it was said ״מִזְבַּח אֲדָמָה תַּעֲשֶׂה לִּי״ (Exodus 20) — would that it serve him as atonement and he be able to stand." "<b>And He breathed into his nostrils.</b> He made him both from the lower [realms] and from the upper — body from the lower, and soul from the upper. For on the first day heaven and earth were created; on the second, He made the firmament for the upper; on the third, let the dry land appear — for the lower; on the fourth, He made luminaries for the upper; on the fifth, let the waters swarm — for the lower. He was compelled on the sixth to create in it both upper and lower — for were it not so, there would be jealousy in the work of Creation, these being greater than those in the creation of a single day." "<b>A living soul.</b> Even beast and wild animal are called נֶפֶשׁ חַיָּה — but this one of man is the life of them all, for knowledge and speech were added in him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:16.679198782Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}